    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily on favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms today, with **Trevor Story** leading the way at a 73.92 efficiency score. **Story** benefits from a distinct park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez, amplified by wind conditions blowing out that should heighten his power potential. We are also high on **Corbin Carroll** (68.74) and **James Wood** (68.42); **Wood** is particularly well-positioned in the leadoff spot against Sandy Alcantara, where his elite xwOBA and the pitcher's slower delivery to the plate provide a prime environment for him to leverage his speed. **Tyler Soderstrom** (63.88) also warrants attention, as he faces a soft matchup against Akin in a high-scoring park environment that allows his power profile to flourish despite a modest platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Travis Bazzana**, whose 44.91 score landed him just outside the active roster. While **Bazzana** possesses a strong xwOBA of .382, he was edged out by the superior lineup positioning and higher dynamic platoon adjustments afforded to **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor**. Further down the depth chart, we opted to bench **Mickey Moniak** (39.40), as the threat of a sub-40 efficiency score\u2014driven by a brutal matchup against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez and an unfavorable platoon split\u2014necessitated a move to the bench to preserve our game cap allotment. \n\nOwners should monitor the risk profile of **Seiya Suzuki** (44.97) and **Jose Caballero** (41.62) closely. Both face elite arms in deGrom and Henderson, respectively, where suppressed strikeout-to-walk ratios and defensive considerations have significantly dampened their outlooks. Furthermore, the aggressive base-running upside of players like **Carroll** and **Wood** will be challenged by elite catcher pop times, which has served as a minor de-rating factor in today\u2019s projections. We are banking on the high-floor production of **Pasquantino** and **Naylor** to stabilize the lineup while we wait for the high-ceiling gambles like **Story** and **Wood** to provide the necessary spark in the SB and HR categories.",
